### Human: Can you write a pop-up window to remind us to clean up the computer regularly?
### Assistant: I can help you create a pop-up window to remind users to clean up their computer regularly. Here's an example using HTML and CSS:
```
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Auto-Clean Reminder</title>
	<style>
		body {
			font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
			background-color: #f2f2f2;
		}
		Reminder {
			position: fixed;
			top: 50%;
			left: 50%;
			transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
			background-color: #333;
			color: #fff;
			padding: 20px;
			border-radius: 10px;
			width: 300px;
			max-width: 400px;
			position: absolute;
			z-index: 1;
		}
		Reminder h2 {
			margin-top: 0;
		}
		Reminder p {
			margin-bottom: 10px;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="Reminder">
		<h2>Auto-Clean Reminder</h2>
		<p>Don't forget to clean up your computer regularly!</p>
		<p>Click here to schedule a reminder.</p>
		<button>Close</button>
	</div>
	<script>
		// Get the pop-up window
		var reminderWindow = document.querySelector('.Reminder');

		// Function to schedule a reminder
		function scheduleReminder(topic, frequency) {
			// Set the reminder for the specified frequency
			reminderWindow.innerHTML = `<h2>Reminder: ${topic}</h2><p>Will be sent at ${frequency} time(s).</p><button>Close</button>`;

			// Add an event listener to the close button
			reminderWindow.querySelector('button').addEventListener('click', function(e) {
				e.preventDefault();
				reminderWindow.outerHTML = '';
			});
		}

		// Set the reminder for automatic cleaning
		scheduleReminder('Computer', 'daily');
	</script>
</body>
</html>
```
This code creates a simple pop-up window with a reminder message. The code uses HTML for structure and CSS for styling. The JavaScript function `scheduleReminder` sets the reminder message and adds an event listener to the close button.

